Subject: [RFC v1 0/2] dt-bindings: arm:asr + ARM: dts: asr1826s-kagu skeleton (Ooredoo R291 v2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This is a Request-For-Comment series shipping the first upstream-able
artifacts for the ASR Microelectronics ASR1802S SoC (board "KAGU"), as
found in the Ooredoo R291 v2 IAD gateway.  The SoC is **not supported by
mainline Linux today** — every peripheral (UART/PCIe/SPI-NAND/eth/USB)
runs from a vendor kernel 3.10.33 fork (OpenWrt BB 14.07 target
`mmp/asr1826s`) and WiFi is a binary-only `rtl8192cd.ko`.

Purpose of this RFC: get the DT binding + board skeleton on-list so the
following SoC-port series (clock/reset/pinctrl/irq/SPI-NAND/PCIe/eth to
linux-arm) can be scoped *before* attempting a full mainline port.

Series content:
  - 1/2: YAML DT bindings for `asr,1802s` (SoC) and `ooredoo,r291-v2`
         (board) — every MMIO/IRQ/flash-partition value is annotated to
         its runtime source (/proc/iomem, /proc/interrupts, /proc/mtd,
         and the U-Boot env on mtd21).
  - 2/2: a minimal board DTS (`asr1826s-kagu`) + an `asr1802s.dtsi` SoC
         stub whose clock/irq/timer nodes are placeholders to be
         back-filled from vendor sources.

Nothing here modifies the running box: all data is extracted with a root
shell (paramiko) + U-Boot env and bit-exact `rootfs-a.bin`/`kernel-a.bin`
backups kept in `ooredoo_backup/` for recovery.  Validate (no NAND
writes) with a Cortex-A9 initramfs.itb + `tftp 0x8000 …; bootm` from the
Marvell `mrvlboot` U-Boot (bootdelay=1).

